  annotation = {中文辅助译名：通过域敏感时空特征丢失进行基于脑电图的广义情绪识别},
  abstract = {Due to substantial individual differences, cross-subject electroencephalography (EEG)-based emotion recognition presents significant challenges. By extracting domain-invariant features from multiple source domains, domain generalization techniques enhance model performance on unseen target data and offer a practical remedy for this problem. However, existing approaches typically align the feature space by adding additional regularization terms, which may distort the original feature distribution and impair discriminative ability for emotional categories. Instead of altering feature distribution, in this work we introduce a Domain-Sensitive Spatio-Temporal Feature Dropout (DSTFdrop) model which proactively detects and removes features highly sensitive to domain shifts, thereby guiding the feature extractor to learn a more robust feature subset while maintaining the feature space unchanged. The model uses graph convolutional networks (GCN) to extract spatial domain features and gated recurrent units (GRU) to extract temporal domain features. Two domain discriminators are deployed to detect spatial and temporal features that are sensitive to domain shifts. Weight scores generated by these two discriminators pinpoint unstable features across specific time steps or EEG channels. These unstable features are dynamically dropped during training, which effectively prunes domain-specific variations without distorting the overall feature space. Extensive assessments verify the effective},
}

